  "source_reconstruction": {
    "address_schedule": "Initial allocation order and free policy are source-complete, but the exact realized sequence is a function of scheduler batch membership, DCP chunks, radix eviction, accepted draft depth, and free timing. Those events are absent from the bound trace. The physical conclusion does not assume a replacement synthetic schedule: it quantifies all integer slot permutations.",
    "alignment": "Each K or V slot row is 16*256=4096 E5M2 bytes. Selecting any head adds a 256-byte-aligned offset. Every 256-byte head slice therefore occupies exactly eight 32-byte sectors and two 128-byte transactions regardless of the slot integer.",
    "decode_consumer": "GQA decode selects the grouped kernel. BLOCK_H=16 groups the two query heads per KV head; with 16 KV heads and eight configured splits, the split CTAs collectively consume each request's index stream 16 times and request each KV-head payload once.",
    "extend_consumer": "Hopper head_dim 256 selects BLOCK_M=64, BLOCK_N=64, eight warps. The grid has one CTA per request, query head, and M tile. A 12-query NGRAM target-verification block fits one M tile, so each of 32 query-head CTAs loads one int64 index stream; paired query heads request the same KV-head payload.",
    "metadata_producer": "update_sliding_window_buffer gathers the last min(seq_len,1023) int32 req_to_token entries into an int64 window_kv_indices buffer and translates them through the int64 full_to_swa map.",
    "ownership": "ReqToTokenPool is int32 [request_row, logical_position]. At page size one, common.alloc_for_extend/decode calls the token allocator, which slices the head of free_pages; frees append or enter release_pages depending on need_sort. SWA allocation pairs a full slot with a separately allocated SWA slot in an int64 full_to_swa mapping.",
    "producer": "Gemma4Attention sends canonical K/V through TritonAttnBackend._set_kv_buffer. SWAKVPool selects the local layer buffer and MHATokenToKVPool stores E5M2 at [swa_slot, kv_head, head_dim]."
  },
